        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willowdale%2C_Toronto"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Gibson House, built in 1851, still stands at 5172 Yonge Street and now serves as a historic house museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willowdale%2C_Toronto"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before becoming Willowdale, the village was known as Kummer’s Settlement, a small community on Yonge Street nine miles from York.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://westwillowdale.com/membership-resources/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Willowdale began as a postal village covering Finch to Elmwood and Bathurst to Bayview, shaping its early layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willowdale%2C_Toronto"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the 1990s, the neighborhood saw a boom of large two‑storey luxury homes replacing smaller houses on the same lots.",
